cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PeerKV: Compute Follows the KV — NVLink KV-Parallel Attention and Peer-GPU Tiering for Long-Context LLM Inference"
message: "Cite as below."
authors:
  - given-names: Chet
    family-names: Li
type: software
abstract: >
  PeerKV makes peer-GPU HBM over NVLink a first-class near tier for an LLM
  KV cache that overflows a single GPU. It contributes a calibrated
  cross-tier cost model, a closed-form schedulability sizing inversion, and a
  topology-aware placement policy; the headline mechanism is
  "compute follows the KV": instead of moving cold KV back over NVLink, each
  GPU computes its shard's attention partial locally and only the ~KB
  online-softmax statistics cross the link (numerically exact, ring/flash
  merge). Measured on a dual-A100 NVLink server. The Python package is
  imported as `umallm` (historical module name).
license: Apache-2.0
